# Zeldapro project rules

## Source of truth

- **Company copy, services (9), AI solutions (6), industries (8), pages, and homepage sections:** `docs/BRIEF.md`
- **Design tokens, layout decisions, and visual iteration notes:** `docs/DESIGN_LOG.md` (append as work progresses; do not overwrite history)

Read the brief before implementing or changing user-facing content.

## Stack (do not downgrade)

- Vite + React + TypeScript (existing root project only—**no nested apps**)
- Tailwind CSS **v4** via `@tailwindcss/vite` and `@import 'tailwindcss'` in global CSS
- `react-router-dom` for routing
- `framer-motion` for motion
- `lucide-react` for icons
- `react-helmet-async` for document title/meta
- `clsx` for conditional classes

Preserve existing Vite and TypeScript configuration unless a task explicitly requires a minimal, justified change.

## Folder conventions

| Path | Use |
|------|-----|
| `src/components/ui` | Reusable primitives (buttons, inputs, cards) |
| `src/components/layout` | Header, footer, nav, topbar |
| `src/sections` | Composable page sections (especially homepage) |
| `src/pages` | Route-level page components |
| `src/layouts` | App shells and shared layouts |
| `src/data` | Static content arrays/objects sourced from the brief |
| `src/hooks` | Custom React hooks |
| `src/styles` | Global styles and Tailwind-related CSS when split from legacy files |
| `src/assets/images` | Marketing and UI imagery |
| `src/assets/logo` | Approved brand logos |

Prefer data-driven UI: define copy in `src/data`, render in sections/pages.

## Implementation standards

- Match enterprise tone and claims in `docs/BRIEF.md`; no invented clients, metrics, or logos.
- Validate **Carevie** and product claims against approved product facts before publishing.
- Contact / lead forms must POST to `import.meta.env.VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT` (see `.env.example`).
- Use semantic HTML, accessible labels, and keyboard-friendly navigation.
- Brand theme color reference: `#081d29`.
- Keep diffs focused; do not refactor unrelated template code in the same change.

## Environment

- Document required env vars in `.env.example`; never commit secrets.
- Local development uses `.env` (gitignored) mirroring `.env.example`.

## Scope discipline

- Follow the user’s request: setup vs. page build vs. content migration are separate phases.
- When asked only for project setup or configuration, do not implement full pages or marketing UI unless explicitly requested.

## Quality

- Run `npm run lint` after substantive TS/TSX edits.
- Ensure `npm run build` passes before considering a feature complete (when building is in scope).